IMPORT prelude

-- Registration of Births and Deaths Act 2021 (Singapore) -- whether, and on whose request, a father's particulars go into the
-- register of births when the parents are not married to each other: what "birth particulars" are (s 2(1), (2)), who must
-- and who may give them (ss 8(1), 8(1A), 8(5), 9(1)), registration with incomplete particulars (s 9(2)), the parents'
-- particulars in an assisted-reproduction case (s 16), re-registration on legitimation by the parents' later marriage
-- (s 15), adding an omitted particular and correcting an error (ss 38, 40(3)), and the regulation-making power that the
-- answer actually lives under (s 61(2)(a)).
--
-- Edition: Act 17 of 2021, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RBDA2021.txt ("version
-- in force from 30/9/2026"), with amendments by Act 2 of 2024 (in force 16 April 2024) shown.
--
-- WHY. Added on 11 October 2026 for REQ-0272 (Jun Hao scenario, event j051): "A child is born to parents who are not
-- married to each other. May the father's name and particulars be entered in the register, and on whose request?"
-- The expectation was "yes, at the joint request of both parents".
--
-- WHAT THE DEPOSIT SAYS. NOTHING ON THE POINT. The words "father", "married" (of the parents, outside s 15's "marriage of
-- the subject person's parents") and "joint request" do not occur in this Act. There is no provision on registering a
-- father's particulars where the parents are not married. Which particulars are recorded is left to regulations
-- (s 61(2)(a): "particulars to be recorded in registers") and to what the Registrar-General "specifies on a prescribed
-- website" (s 2(1), "birth particulars" (b)), and s 2(2) lets the Registrar-General specify different particulars "for
-- children in different circumstances". The joint-request rule the expectation describes is (from memory, NOT checked
-- against a deposit) the rule of s 10 of the repealed Registration of Births and Deaths Act (Cap. 267), repealed by s 62.
-- Whatever replaced it lives in the Registration of Births and Deaths Regulations or on the Registrar-General's website,
-- neither of which is deposited.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the content of any regulations or of the Registrar-General's website; who is a "parent" (the Act does not
-- define it -- the encoding reads it, as an INFERENCE, to include a biological father whether or not married to the
-- mother); the Legitimacy Act 1934 test of legitimation itself; the Status of Children (Assisted Reproduction Technology)
-- Act 2013 rules of parenthood; s 17 and s 18 re-registration (the ART cases); births in conveyances (ss 11-13); adoption
-- (s 14); clerical errors (s 39); cancellation (s 41); appeals under regulations.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Registration of Births and Deaths Act 2021 -- the father's particulars`

§§ `the question REQ-0272 asks`

-- What the Act ITSELF says about entering a father's particulars, by kind of case. The parents' marriage is an input only
-- so that the cases file can show it makes no difference: no provision of the Act turns on it at first registration.
DECLARE `Act's answer` IS ONE OF
    `as a court order under the ART Act directs`
    `as the ART Act directs`
    `the Registrar-General may register without either or both parents' particulars`
    `the Act does not say: left to regulations and the Registrar-General's website`

-- s 16(1): if the Registrar-General "is informed at or before registration of a child's birth under section 9 or 13 that
-- the Status of Children (Assisted Reproduction Technology) Act 2013 applies to the child, the particulars of the child's
-- parents to be entered in the register of births ... must be -- (a) in the case where a court order is made under that
-- Act declaring or determining the child's parenthood -- in accordance with the court order; or (b) in any other case --
-- subject to subsection (2), in accordance with that Act."
-- s 16(2): (1)(b) does not apply if the Registrar-General "(a) is not satisfied as to the parenthood of the child under
-- [that Act]; or (b) is informed of any dispute as to the parenthood of the child under that Act."
-- s 16(3): if (2)(a) or (b) applies, the Registrar-General may "register the child's birth under section 9(2) ... without
-- entering the particulars of either or both of the parents in the register".
GIVEN `parents married to each other` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `ART Act applies and Registrar-General informed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `ART court order of parenthood` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Registrar-General satisfied as to ART parenthood` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `informed of an ART parenthood dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Act's answer`
`what the Act says about the parents' particulars` MEANS
    IF NOT `ART Act applies and Registrar-General informed`
    THEN `the Act does not say: left to regulations and the Registrar-General's website`
    ELSE IF `ART court order of parenthood`
         THEN `as a court order under the ART Act directs`
         ELSE IF `Registrar-General satisfied as to ART parenthood` AND (NOT `informed of an ART parenthood dispute`)
              THEN `as the ART Act directs`
              ELSE `the Registrar-General may register without either or both parents' particulars`

-- The expectation's rule, tested against the Act: does anything in the Act make a joint request of both parents a
-- condition of entering the father's particulars? No section does, in any case.
GIVEN `parents married to each other` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act requires a joint request of both parents` IF FALSE

§§ `2(1) and 2(2) -- birth particulars`

-- s 2(1): "'birth particulars', for a child, means -- (a) any particulars relating to the child required by or under this
-- Act for the purposes of birth registration; and (b) any other particulars relating to the child that the
-- Registrar-General specifies on a prescribed website for the purposes of birth registration".
-- s 2(2): the Registrar-General may specify "(a) different birth particulars under paragraph (b) ... for children in
-- different circumstances".
-- s 61(2)(a): the Minister may make regulations for "matters relating to registration of births ... including reporting
-- and registration requirements and procedures, particulars to be recorded in registers, recording of particulars in
-- registers after registration, and alteration of records in registers".
DECLARE `Particulars source` IS ONE OF
    `this Act`
    `regulations under section 61`
    `the Registrar-General's prescribed website`
    `somewhere else`

GIVEN `the source` IS A `Particulars source`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `can make something a birth particular` IF
        `the source` EQUALS `this Act`
    OR  `the source` EQUALS `regulations under section 61`
    OR  `the source` EQUALS `the Registrar-General's prescribed website`

§§ `8 and 9(1) -- who must, and who may, give the birth particulars`

DECLARE `Particulars giver` IS ONE OF
    `the father`
    `the mother`
    `a legal guardian`
    `a CYPA protector with naming power`
    `any other person`

-- s 8(5): "'responsible person', for a child, means ... (a) every parent of the child; (b) where the child has a legal
-- guardian, the legal guardian; (c) where the child is the subject of an order under [the Children and Young Persons Act
-- 1993] ... that enables the Director-General of Social Welfare or a protector to make a decision relating to the child's
-- name -- the Director-General of Social Welfare or the protector".
-- INFERENCE: "parent" is undefined; the father counts as "every parent" whether or not married to the mother. The Act
-- gives no ground for reading him out.
GIVEN `the giver` IS A `Particulars giver`, `child has a legal guardian` IS A BOOLEAN, `CYPA naming order made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a responsible person` IF
        `the giver` EQUALS `the father`
    OR  `the giver` EQUALS `the mother`
    OR  (`the giver` EQUALS `a legal guardian` AND `child has a legal guardian`)
    OR  (`the giver` EQUALS `a CYPA protector with naming power` AND `CYPA naming order made`)

-- s 9(1): "The Registrar-General must register the birth of a child born in Singapore, as soon as practicable after
-- receiving the child's birth particulars (whether from a responsible person mentioned in section 8(1) or any other
-- person)." So the Act lets ANYONE give the particulars; it does not ask for a request, joint or single, from anyone.
GIVEN `the giver` IS A `Particulars giver`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may give the birth particulars` IF TRUE

-- s 8(1): a responsible person "must provide to the Registrar-General -- (a) the birth particulars for the child, within 42
-- days after the child's birth". (3): one responsible person's compliance discharges the rest. So the unmarried father
-- shares the duty with the mother, and either one's compliance discharges both.
GIVEN `the giver` IS A `Particulars giver`, `child has a legal guardian` IS A BOOLEAN, `CYPA naming order made` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days since birth` IS A NUMBER, `someone responsible has provided them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `still owes the birth particulars` IF
        `is a responsible person` `the giver` `child has a legal guardian` `CYPA naming order made`
    AND (NOT `someone responsible has provided them`)
    AND `days since birth` AT MOST 42

§§ `8(1A) and 9(2) -- registering with a particular missing`

-- s 9(2): the Registrar-General "may ... register a child's birth despite receiving incomplete birth particulars for the
-- child, if the Registrar-General -- (a) is satisfied that the child is born in Singapore; and (b) is of the opinion that
-- the child's birth is capable of being registered based on the birth particulars available".
GIVEN `satisfied born in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `capable of registration on what is available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may register with incomplete particulars` IF
    `satisfied born in Singapore` AND `capable of registration on what is available`

-- s 8(1A)(b): "where the child's birth is registered without any other birth particular [than the name] -- the duty of a
-- responsible person ... to provide that birth particular continues despite the registration until that birth particular is
-- provided to the Registrar-General". INFERENCE: IF the regulations or the website make the father's particulars a birth
-- particular, a registration without them leaves the duty running. Whether they are one for an unmarried father is the
-- point the Act does not decide.
GIVEN `registered under 9(2) without the particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `the particular since provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty to give the missing particular continues` IF
    `registered under 9(2) without the particular` AND (NOT `the particular since provided`)

§§ `38 and 40(3) -- adding or correcting a particular later`

-- s 38(1): "Any record of a registered event in a register must not be altered except as authorised by or under this Act."
-- (2): alteration "includes ... the recording in the register of the particulars of the registered event that had been
-- omitted from the register at the time of registration".
GIVEN `is adding an omitted particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised by or under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `adding or changing the record is lawful` IF `authorised by or under the Act`

GIVEN `is adding an omitted particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts as an alteration` IF `is adding an omitted particular`

-- s 40(3): "The Registrar-General may correct an error of fact or substance in any record in the register of births ...
-- after receiving a request from any person." (4)-(5): the request must contain and be accompanied by the information and
-- evidence the Registrar-General requires. (6): the Registrar-General may also correct on own volition.
GIVEN `request received` IS A BOOLEAN, `required evidence provided` IS A BOOLEAN, `acting on own volition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may correct an error of fact in the births register` IF
        (`request received` AND `required evidence provided`)
    OR  `acting on own volition`

§§ `15 -- re-registration on legitimation by the parents' later marriage`

-- s 15(1): applies to a person "(a) whose birth is registered under section 9 or 13 (or section 9, 17 or 23 of the repealed
-- Act); and (b) who is legitimated by the Legitimacy Act 1934, on the marriage of the subject person's parents, after the
-- birth registration".
GIVEN `birth registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `legitimated by the parents' marriage after registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 15 applies` IF
    `birth registered` AND `legitimated by the parents' marriage after registration`

DECLARE `s 15 applicant` IS ONE OF
    `a parent`
    `the subject person`
    `someone else`

-- s 15(2): the application may be made "(a) where the subject person is a minor -- a parent of the subject person; (b) where
-- the subject person is not a minor -- (i) the subject person; or (ii) a parent of the subject person, with the consent of
-- the subject person." One parent suffices; the Act does not ask for both.
GIVEN `the applicant` IS A `s 15 applicant`, `subject person is a minor` IS A BOOLEAN, `subject person consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for re-registration on legitimation` IF
    IF `subject person is a minor`
    THEN `the applicant` EQUALS `a parent`
    ELSE     `the applicant` EQUALS `the subject person`
         OR  (`the applicant` EQUALS `a parent` AND `subject person consents`)

-- s 15(3): the application "may include a change of name for the subject person, but only to the extent of altering the
-- subject person's name entered in the register of births to reflect the paternity of the subject person."
-- s 15(5): the Registrar-General "may re-register the birth" if "(a) ... satisfied that -- (i) the applicant has complied
-- with the requirements relating to the application; and (ii) the subject person is legitimated by the Legitimacy Act 1934;
-- and (b) where the application includes a change of name -- (i) the new name complies with the requirements of subsection
-- (3), and with section 19(1); and (ii) the Registrar-General does not refuse the new name under section 19(2)."
GIVEN `applicant complied` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `satisfied legitimated` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `includes a change of name` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `change only reflects paternity` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `new name complies with 19(1)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Registrar-General refuses the name under 19(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may re-register on legitimation` IF
        `applicant complied`
    AND `satisfied legitimated`
    AND (    (NOT `includes a change of name`)
         OR  (    `change only reflects paternity`
              AND `new name complies with 19(1)`
              AND (NOT `Registrar-General refuses the name under 19(2)`)))
